=begin
      author: Scott
        name: deadexit
        game: gemstone
        tags: safety, bigshot
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 0.1
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Unattended-death safety net for bigshot hunts.

  bigshot's dead_man_switch() always runs while ;bigshot is active, but unless
  its profile has "Dead man's switch" (GSF only) or "Depart/rerun if dead"
  turned on, its default behavior on death is just to kill the bigshot script
  -- it leaves you connected, dead, sitting in the room. Fine if you're
  watching, but bad if you're AFK: you decay, and anyone who wanders by can
  raise/resurrect you while you're not there to say no to it.

  This script watches for you dying while ;bigshot is (or was just) running
  and quits the game outright, so an AFK session ends in a clean logout
  instead of a decaying, rezzable corpse. It doesn't touch bigshot's own
  Dead man's switch / Depart-rerun settings -- those still fire first; this
  is a belt-and-suspenders exit for whatever bigshot leaves behind.

  Gated by the UserVar afk_now, which defaults ON. When you're actually at
  the keyboard doing interactive hunting and would rather handle your own
  death yourself (get rezzed, keep playing), turn it off for the session:

    ;vars set afk_now=false

  and flip it back on before you walk away again:

    ;vars set afk_now=true

  Meant to be autostarted for every character:

    ;autostart add --global deadexit

  Usage:  ;deadexit
  Stop:   ;kill deadexit
=end

module DeadExit
  # === config =====================================================================
  BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME    = "bigshot"
  CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS = 3
  BIGSHOT_GRACE_SECONDS  = 20 # bridges bigshot self-killing on death just before we poll

  # === helpers ====================================================================

  # afk_now defaults ON (unset counts as on). A real boolean set via
  # `;vars set afk_now=true/false` is honored directly; any other stored
  # string only counts as OFF when it's explicitly one of false/off/no/0
  # (case-insensitive) -- everything else, including unrecognized text, stays ON.
  def self.afk_now?
    value = UserVars.afk_now
    return true if value.nil?
    return value if value == true || value == false

    value.to_s !~ /\A\s*(?:0|false|off|no)\s*\z/i
  end

  # === main =======================================================================
  def self.run
    echo "deadexit started! Watching for death while ;#{BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME} is running (afk_now defaults ON)."
    echo "Hunting interactively? ;vars set afk_now=false to stop the auto-quit."
    echo "Stop with ;kill deadexit"

    bigshot_last_seen = nil

    loop do
      bigshot_last_seen = Time.now if Script.running?(BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME)
      bigshot_recently_hunting = bigshot_last_seen && (Time.now - bigshot_last_seen) < BIGSHOT_GRACE_SECONDS

      if dead? && bigshot_recently_hunting && afk_now?
        echo "deadexit: you're dead and afk_now is on -- quitting so you don't decay or get rezzed unattended."
        fput "quit"
      end

      sleep CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS
    end
  end
end

DeadExit.run
